-wrap:wrap;gap:var(--s-3);padding-bottom:var(--s-4);border-bottom:1px solid var(--tk-rule)"><h1 style="font-size:var(--t-xl)">2013 HONDA Accord</h1><span class="label data">rpt_demo-01 / 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z / mode: fixture</span></header><div style="margin-top:var(--s-5)"><div class="panel panel-edge prose-sm" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-locked)">Automated analysis of media you provided. This is not an inspection, a certification, or a warranty. Confidence is not certainty. Have an independent mechanic examine any vehicle before you buy it. <a href="/accuracy">See how accurate TIREKICK actually is, including the misses.</a></div></div><div class="panel prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3);border-color:var(--tk-locked);color:var(--tk-locked)">This report was generated from synthetic fixture media. The images are drawings, not photographs, and no statement here about condition describes a real vehicle. The federal records below are real: the VIN carries genuine manufacturer codes with an invented serial, so it decodes to a real model and identifies nobody’s car.</div><section class="section" id="coverage"><div class="section-label"><span>What was looked at</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(320px, 100%), auto));gap:var(--s-6);align-items:start"><svg viewBox="0 0 260 360" role="img" aria-label="Coverage map of the vehicle. 7 regions flagged, 3 photographed with nothing flagged, 2 never photographed. 4 systems locked and never assessed remotely: brakes, steering, restraints, structure." style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;max-width:320px"><defs><pattern id="tk-locked-hatch" width="6" height="6" patternTransform="rotate(45)" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="6" stroke="var(--tk-locked)" stroke-width="1.2"></line></pattern></defs><rect x="8" y="4" width="244" height="352" fill="none" stroke="var(--tk-locked)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3 5"></rect><text x="130" y="352" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--tk-display);font-size:7.5px;letter-spacing:0.14em;fill:var(--tk-locked)">STRUCTURE / LOCKED</text><rect x="16" y="62" width="44" height="46" fill="color-mix(in srgb, var(--tk-sev-minor) 18%, transparent)" stroke="var(--tk-sev-minor)" stroke-width="1.25"></rect><rect x="200" y="62" width="44" height="46" fill="color-mix(in srgb, var(--tk-sev-minor) 18%, transparent)" stroke="var(--tk-sev-minor)" stroke-width="1.25"></rect><rect x="16" y="248" width="44" height="46" fill="color-mix(in srgb, var(--tk-sev-minor) 18%, transparent)" stroke="var(--tk-sev-minor)" stroke-width="1.25"></rect><rect x="200" y="248" width="44" height="46" fill="color-mix(in srgb, var(--tk-sev-minor) 18%, transparent)" stroke="var(--tk-sev-minor)" stroke-width="1.25"></rect><g><rect x="72" y="8" width="116" height="46" fill="transparent" stroke="var(--tk-paper)" stroke-width="1.25"></rect><text x="130" y="34" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--tk-display);font-size:8px;letter-spacing:0.1em;fill:var(--tk-paper)">FRONT</text></g><g><rect x="72" y="58" width="116" height="48" fill="color-mix(in srgb, var(--tk-sev-minor) 18%, transparent)" stroke="var(--tk-sev-minor)" stroke-width="1.25"></rect><text x="130" y="81" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--tk-display);font-size:8px;letter-spacing:0.1em;fill:var(--tk-sev-minor)">ENGINE BAY</text><text x="130" y="93" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--tk-mono);font-size:8px;fill:var(--tk-sev-minor)">1 finding</text></g><g><rect x="72" y="110" width="116" height="30" fill="color-mix(in srgb, var(--tk-sev-major) 18%, transparent)" stroke="var(--tk-sev-major)" stroke-width="1.25"></rect><text x="130" y="124" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--tk-display);font-size:8px;letter-spacing:0.1em;fill:var(--tk-sev-major)">DASH</text><text x="130" y="136" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--tk-mono);font-size:8px;fill:var(--tk-sev-major)">1 finding</text></g><g><rect x="72" y="144" width="116" height="60" fill="color-mix(in srgb, var(--tk-sev-minor) 18%, transparent)" stroke="var(--tk-sev-minor)" stroke-width="1.25"></rect><text x="130" y="173" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--tk-display);font-size:8px;letter-spacing:0.1em;fill:var(--tk-sev-minor)">INTERIOR FRONT</text><text x="130" y="185" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--tk-mono);font-size:8px;fill:var(--tk-sev-minor)">1 finding</text></g><g><rect x="72" y="208" width="116" height="54" fill="transparent" stroke="var(--tk-unknown)" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-dasharray="3 4"></rect><text x="130" y="238" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--tk-display);font-size:8px;letter-spacing:0.1em;fill:var(--tk-unknown)">INTERIOR REAR</text></g><g><rect x="72" y="266" width="116" height="46" fill="color-mix(in srgb, var(--tk-sev-minor) 18%, transparent)" stroke="var(--tk-sev-minor)" stroke-width="1.25"></rect><text x="130" y="288" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--tk-display);font-size:8px;letter-spacing:0.1em;fill:var(--tk-sev-minor)">REAR</text><text x="130" y="300" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--tk-mono);font-size:8px;fill:var(--tk-sev-minor)">1 finding</text></g><g><rect x="16" y="118" width="44" height="120" fill="color-mix(in srgb, var(--tk-sev-major) 18%, transparent)" stroke="var(--tk-sev-major)" stroke-width="1.25"></rect><text x="38" y="177" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--tk-display);font-size:8px;letter-spacing:0.1em;fill:var(--tk-sev-major)">LEFT</text><text x="38" y="189" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--tk-mono);font-size:8px;fill:var(--tk-sev-major)">1 finding</text></g><g><rect x="200" y="118" width="44" height="120" fill="transparent" stroke="var(--tk-paper)" stroke-width="1.25"></rect><text x="222" y="181" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--tk-display);font-size:8px;letter-spacing:0.1em;fill:var(--tk-paper)">RIGHT</text></g><g><rect x="44" y="64" width="12" height="12" fill="url(#tk-locked-hatch)" stroke="var(--tk-locked)" stroke-width="1"></rect><title>Brakes: not remotely verifiable, independent mechanic required</title></g><g><rect x="228" y="64" width="12" height="12" fill="url(#tk-locked-hatch)" stroke="var(--tk-locked)" stroke-width="1"></rect><title>Brakes: not remotely verifiable, independent mechanic required</title></g><g><rect x="44" y="250" width="12" height="12" fill="url(#tk-locked-hatch)" stroke="var(--tk-locked)" stroke-width="1"></rect><title>Brakes: not remotely verifiable, independent mechanic required</title></g><g><rect x="228" y="250" width="12" height="12" fill="url(#tk-locked-hatch)" stroke="var(--tk-locked)" stroke-width="1"></rect><title>Brakes: not remotely verifiable, independent mechanic required</title></g><g><rect x="174" y="112" width="12" height="12" fill="url(#tk-locked-hatch)" stroke="var(--tk-locked)" stroke-width="1"></rect><title>Steering: not remotely verifiable, independent mechanic required</title></g><g><rect x="174" y="146" width="12" height="12" fill="url(#tk-locked-hatch)" stroke="var(--tk-locked)" stroke-width="1"></rect><title>Restraints: not remotely verifiable, independent mechanic required</title></g></svg><div><div style="display:grid;gap:var(--s-4)"><div style="display:flex;gap:var(--s-3);align-items:flex-start"><span style="margin-top:4px"><span aria-hidden="true" style="display:inline-block;width:24px;height:15px;border:1.5px solid var(--tk-sev-major);background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--tk-sev-major) 18%, transparent);flex:0 0 auto"></span></span><div><div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:var(--s-2)"><span class="data" style="font-size:var(--t-md)">7</span><span class="label" style="color:var(--tk-paper)">Flagged</span></div><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin:2px 0 0;font-size:var(--t-sm)">A finding cites a photograph of this region. Every one is listed below with the picture it came from.</p></div></div><div style="display:flex;gap:var(--s-3);align-items:flex-start"><span style="margin-top:4px"><span aria-hidden="true" style="display:inline-block;width:24px;height:15px;border:1.5px solid var(--tk-paper);background:transparent;flex:0 0 auto"></span></span><div><div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:var(--s-2)"><span class="data" style="font-size:var(--t-md)">3</span><span class="label" style="color:var(--tk-paper)">Photographed, nothing flagged</span></div><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin:2px 0 0;font-size:var(--t-sm)">An image arrived and a pass ran over it. Nothing adverse was visible. That is a statement about the photograph and not a pass.</p></div></div><div style="display:flex;gap:var(--s-3);align-items:flex-start"><span style="margin-top:4px"><span aria-hidden="true" style="display:inline-block;width:24px;height:15px;border:1.5px dashed var(--tk-unknown);background:transparent;flex:0 0 auto"></span></span><div><div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:var(--s-2)"><span class="data" style="font-size:var(--t-md)">2</span><span class="label" style="color:var(--tk-paper)">Never photographed</span></div><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin:2px 0 0;font-size:var(--t-sm)">No image of this reached us. Nothing in this report describes what it would have shown.</p></div></div><div style="display:flex;gap:var(--s-3);align-items:flex-start"><span style="margin-top:4px"><span aria-hidden="true" style="display:inline-block;width:24px;height:15px;border:1.5px solid var(--tk-locked);background:repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, var(--tk-locked) 0 1.2px, transparent 1.2px 5px);flex:0 0 auto"></span></span><div><div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:var(--s-2)"><span class="data" style="font-size:var(--t-md)">4</span><span class="label" style="color:var(--tk-paper)">Locked</span></div><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin:2px 0 0;font-size:var(--t-sm)">Never assessed remotely, on any vehicle, at any confidence. An independent mechanic is the only route to an answer. <span style="color:var(--tk-locked)">brakes, steering, restraints, structure.</span></p></div></div></div><div style="margin-top:var(--s-5)"><div class="label">Views with no place on a plan view</div><div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:var(--s-2);margin-top:var(--s-2)"><span class="chip" style="color:var(--tk-paper);border-style:solid">Three-quarter</span><span class="chip" style="color:var(--tk-sev-info);border-style:solid">Odometer</span><span class="chip" style="color:var(--tk-unknown);border-style:dashed">VIN plate</span></div></div><p class="prose-sm muted" style="margin-top:var(--s-4);margin-bottom:0">13 photos covering 10 of 12 standard views. Not covered: interior rear, vin plate. Nothing in this report describes what those views would have shown.</p></div></div></section><section class="section" id="verdict"><div class="section-label"><span>Verdict</span></div><div class="panel"><div class="split split-metric" style="gap:var(--s-6)"><div><div class="label">Red-flag score</div><div class="data" style="font-size:var(--t-3xl);line-height:1;color:var(--tk-sev-major)">50<span class="dim" style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">/100</span></div><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin:var(--s-3) 0 0">Severity and confidence of what was visible. Not a grade, and not a statement about the vehicle overall.</p></div><div style="min-width:0"><p class="prose" style="margin:0;font-size:var(--t-lg)">2 finding(s) that are likely to cost money. Separately, 5 recall campaign(s) are on record for this model year - free to fix, and worth one phone call to a dealer.</p><p class="prose-sm muted" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)">13 photos covering 10 of 12 standard views. Not covered: interior rear, vin plate. Nothing in this report describes what those views would have shown. Red-flag score 50/100, which reflects the severity and confidence of what was visible on this vehicle - not the condition of the vehicle overall. Recalls and owner complaint patterns describe the model rather than this car, so they are reported separately and are not counted in the score.</p></div></div><div style="margin-top:var(--s-5);padding-top:var(--s-5);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule)"><div class="label" style="color:var(--tk-locked)">What this analysis could not assess</div><ul class="prose-sm" style="margin:var(--s-3) 0 0;padding-left:0;list-style:none;display:grid;gap:var(--s-3)"><li style="border-left:2px solid var(--tk-locked);padding-left:var(--s-3)">Brakes - not remotely verifiable, independent mechanic required.</li><li style="border-left:2px solid var(--tk-locked);padding-left:var(--s-3)">Airbags and restraints - not remotely verifiable, independent mechanic required.</li><li style="border-left:2px solid var(--tk-locked);padding-left:var(--s-3)">Frame and structural integrity - not remotely verifiable, independent mechanic required.</li><li style="border-left:2px solid var(--tk-locked);padding-left:var(--s-3)">Steering - not remotely verifiable, independent mechanic required.</li><li style="border-left:2px solid var(--tk-locked);padding-left:var(--s-3)">2 standard view(s) were not provided: interior rear, vin plate.</li><li style="border-left:2px solid var(--tk-locked);padding-left:var(--s-3)">TIREKICK does not make claims about engine condition from audio. The anomaly detector has not been measured against a labelled set, so under our own accuracy rules it cannot appear in a report. What is below is the recording itself, drawn as a spectrogram, and the measurements taken from it. Listen to the clip yourself, and play it to a mechanic at a cold start.</li><li style="border-left:2px solid var(--tk-locked);padding-left:var(--s-3)">Title status - TIREKICK queries no title registry. Any title brand named in this report was read out of paperwork you uploaded. Confirm the title with your state motor vehicle agency before you buy.</li><li style="border-left:2px solid var(--tk-locked);padding-left:var(--s-3)">5 frame(s) were taken from 14 seconds of video and analysed as photographs. 4 were too blurred to read - a blurred frame is worse than no frame, because it is the input most likely to turn a shadow into a dent. 4 showed the same view as a frame already chosen.</li></ul></div></div></section><section class="section" id="findings"><div class="section-label"><span>Findings about this vehicle (8)</span><span class="dim" style="letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:none">worst first</span></div><div style="display:grid;gap:var(--s-4)"><article id="vf_lamp_01" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-sev-major)"><header style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--s-3)"><span class="chip chip-solid" style="background:var(--tk-sev-major)">major</span><span class="label">Dash Warning Light · vision</span></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="CONF 0.83"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">CONF</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-major)">0.83</span></span></header><div class="split split-figure" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)"><div style="display:grid;gap:var(--s-3)"><figure style="margin:0"><a href="#asset-photo_05" style="display:block;text-decoration:none"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;background:#000;border:1px solid var(--tk-rule);aspect-ratio:1.5"><img src="/f/demo-01/photo_05.jpg" alt="Cropped region of photo_05: Illuminated lamp in the instrument cluster" style="position:absolute;width:407.4074%;height:458.3333%;left:-222.9630%;top:-115.0000%;max-width:none"/><span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:29.6296%;top:22.5000%;width:40.7407%;height:55.0000%;border:2px solid var(--tk-sev-major);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.55)"><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;top:-2px;left:-2px;border-top:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major);border-left:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;top:-2px;right:-2px;border-top:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major);border-right:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;bottom:-2px;left:-2px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major);border-left:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;bottom:-2px;right:-2px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major);border-right:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major)"></span></span><span class="label" style="position:absolute;top:8px;left:8px;background:var(--tk-locked);color:var(--tk-void);font-size:9px;padding:2px 6px">Synthetic</span><span class="data" style="position:absolute;bottom:8px;right:8px;background:rgba(11,10,9,0.82);color:var(--tk-graphite);font-size:10px;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid var(--tk-rule)">4.1×</span></div></a><figcaption style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-3);margin-top:var(--s-2);font-size:var(--t-xs)"><span class="data dim">photo_05</span><span class="dim" style="text-align:right">10×12% of frame</span></figcaption></figure></div><div style="min-width:0"><h3 style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">Check-engine lamp illuminated in the instrument cluster</h3><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">A check-engine lamp is illuminated in the cluster in this photograph. What triggered it cannot be determined without reading the fault codes with a scan tool.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)"><strong style="font-weight:600">Why this confidence:</strong> The lamp shape and position are clearly legible. The reading is about the photograph, not about the vehicle&#x27;s condition.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-2);font-size:var(--t-sm)">Illuminated lamp in the instrument cluster <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">photo_05 [0.62, 0.30, 0.10, 0.12]</span></p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule);display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask the seller</span> The check-engine light is on in your photo. What code is it throwing, and how long has it been on?</div><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask a mechanic</span> Have the fault codes read with a scan tool before agreeing on a price. A $20 code read can be the difference between a sensor and a catalytic converter.</div></div></div></div></article><article id="vf_rust_01" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-sev-major)"><header style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--s-3)"><span class="chip chip-solid" style="background:var(--tk-sev-major)">major</span><span class="label">Rust Corrosion · vision</span></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="CONF 0.72"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">CONF</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-major)">0.72</span></span></header><div class="split split-figure" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)"><div style="display:grid;gap:var(--s-3)"><figure style="margin:0"><a href="#asset-photo_01" style="display:block;text-decoration:none"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;background:#000;border:1px solid var(--tk-rule);aspect-ratio:1.5"><img src="/f/demo-01/photo_01.jpg" alt="Cropped region of photo_01: Corrosion band along the lower rocker panel" style="position:absolute;width:161.7647%;height:181.9853%;left:0.0000%;top:-75.5699%;max-width:none"/><span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:12.9412%;top:37.2610%;width:55.0000%;height:25.4779%;border:2px solid var(--tk-sev-major);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.55)"><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;top:-2px;left:-2px;border-top:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major);border-left:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;top:-2px;right:-2px;border-top:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major);border-right:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;bottom:-2px;left:-2px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major);border-left:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;bottom:-2px;right:-2px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major);border-right:3px solid var(--tk-sev-major)"></span></span><span class="label" style="position:absolute;top:8px;left:8px;background:var(--tk-locked);color:var(--tk-void);font-size:9px;padding:2px 6px">Synthetic</span><span class="data" style="position:absolute;bottom:8px;right:8px;background:rgba(11,10,9,0.82);color:var(--tk-graphite);font-size:10px;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid var(--tk-rule)">1.6×</span></div></a><figcaption style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-3);margin-top:var(--s-2);font-size:var(--t-xs)"><span class="data dim">photo_01</span><span class="dim" style="text-align:right">34×14% of frame</span></figcaption></figure></div><div style="min-width:0"><h3 style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">Corrosion visible along driver-side rocker panel</h3><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">A band of corrosion is visible along the lower rocker panel, roughly one third of the panel length. The texture in this image is consistent with surface corrosion rather than perforation, but whether the metal is compromised underneath cannot be determined from a photograph.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)"><strong style="font-weight:600">Why this confidence:</strong> The region is well lit and unobstructed. Confidence is held below 0.8 because surface corrosion and early perforation look similar at this resolution.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-2);font-size:var(--t-sm)">Corrosion band along the lower rocker panel <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">photo_01 [0.08, 0.62, 0.34, 0.14]</span></p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule);display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Est. repair</span> <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-sev-major)">$600–$900</span></div><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask the seller</span> How long has the rust on the rocker panel been there, and has any bodywork been done to it?</div><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask a mechanic</span> Ask a mechanic to probe the rocker panel and inspect the seam from underneath on a lift.</div></div></div></div></article><article id="title_hail_history_01" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-sev-minor)"><header style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--s-3)"><span class="chip chip-solid" style="background:var(--tk-sev-minor)">minor</span><span class="label">Title Brand Indicator · data</span></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="CONF 1.00"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">CONF</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-minor)">1.00</span></span></header><div class="split" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)"><div style="min-width:0"><h3 style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">Hail damage reported in your documents</h3><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">A document you uploaded reports hail damage. The line is quoted below exactly as it appears. Usually cosmetic, and usually reflected in the price already. TIREKICK did not query any title registry - this is a reading of your own paperwork, and paperwork can be incomplete or forged. Confirm the brand with your state&#x27;s motor vehicle agency before you buy, and price the car as branded until you have.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)"><strong style="font-weight:600">Why this confidence:</strong> Exact text matching against the document you provided, not a model judgment. What is certain is that the quoted line appears in your document. Whether the document is complete, current, or genuine is not something TIREKICK can check.</p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule)"><div class="label">Evidence</div><ul class="prose-sm" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 0;padding-left:var(--s-5)"><li class="dim" style="margin-bottom:var(--s-1)"><span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-paper)">history_01</span> — “2019-04 Hail damage reported to insurer. Roof and hood panels replaced.”</li></ul></div><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule);display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask the seller</span> My paperwork mentions hail damage. Can you walk me through what happened, and show me the title itself?</div><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask a mechanic</span> Tell the mechanic what the paperwork says before the inspection - it changes what they look at first.</div></div></div></div></article><article id="vf_wear_01" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-sev-minor)"><header style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--s-3)"><span class="chip chip-solid" style="background:var(--tk-sev-minor)">minor</span><span class="label">Interior Wear · vision</span></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="CONF 0.78"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">CONF</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-minor)">0.78</span></span></header><div class="split split-figure" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)"><div style="display:grid;gap:var(--s-3)"><figure style="margin:0"><a href="#asset-photo_04" style="display:block;text-decoration:none"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;background:#000;border:1px solid var(--tk-rule);aspect-ratio:1.5"><img src="/f/demo-01/photo_04.jpg" alt="Cropped region of photo_04: Outer driver seat bolster" style="position:absolute;width:222.2222%;height:250.0000%;left:-21.1111%;top:-90.0000%;max-width:none"/><span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:23.3333%;top:22.5000%;width:53.3333%;height:55.0000%;border:2px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.55)"><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;top:-2px;left:-2px;border-top:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-left:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;top:-2px;right:-2px;border-top:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-right:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;bottom:-2px;left:-2px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-left:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;bottom:-2px;right:-2px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-right:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span></span><span class="label" style="position:absolute;top:8px;left:8px;background:var(--tk-locked);color:var(--tk-void);font-size:9px;padding:2px 6px">Synthetic</span><span class="data" style="position:absolute;bottom:8px;right:8px;background:rgba(11,10,9,0.82);color:var(--tk-graphite);font-size:10px;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid var(--tk-rule)">2.2×</span></div></a><figcaption style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-3);margin-top:var(--s-2);font-size:var(--t-xs)"><span class="data dim">photo_04</span><span class="dim" style="text-align:right">24×22% of frame</span></figcaption></figure></div><div style="min-width:0"><h3 style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">Driver seat bolster wear</h3><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">Wear is visible on the outer driver seat bolster, consistent with regular entry and exit over time. No tearing is visible.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)"><strong style="font-weight:600">Why this confidence:</strong> Bolster wear is one of the more reliably visible interior signals in a well-lit cabin photo.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-2);font-size:var(--t-sm)">Outer driver seat bolster <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">photo_04 [0.20, 0.45, 0.24, 0.22]</span></p></div></div></article><article id="vf_dent_01" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-sev-minor)"><header style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--s-3)"><span class="chip chip-solid" style="background:var(--tk-sev-minor)">minor</span><span class="label">Exterior Damage · vision</span></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="CONF 0.64"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">CONF</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-minor)">0.64</span></span></header><div class="split split-figure" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)"><div style="display:grid;gap:var(--s-3)"><figure style="margin:0"><a href="#asset-photo_03" style="display:block;text-decoration:none"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;background:#000;border:1px solid var(--tk-rule);aspect-ratio:1.5"><img src="/f/demo-01/photo_03.jpg" alt="Cropped region of photo_03: Deformation above the rear wheel arch" style="position:absolute;width:271.6049%;height:305.5556%;left:-126.5432%;top:-99.7222%;max-width:none"/><span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:22.8395%;top:22.5000%;width:54.3210%;height:55.0000%;border:2px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.55)"><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;top:-2px;left:-2px;border-top:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-left:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;top:-2px;right:-2px;border-top:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-right:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;bottom:-2px;left:-2px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-left:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;bottom:-2px;right:-2px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-right:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span></span><span class="label" style="position:absolute;top:8px;left:8px;background:var(--tk-locked);color:var(--tk-void);font-size:9px;padding:2px 6px">Synthetic</span><span class="data" style="position:absolute;bottom:8px;right:8px;background:rgba(11,10,9,0.82);color:var(--tk-graphite);font-size:10px;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid var(--tk-rule)">2.7×</span></div></a><figcaption style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-3);margin-top:var(--s-2);font-size:var(--t-xs)"><span class="data dim">photo_03</span><span class="dim" style="text-align:right">20×18% of frame</span></figcaption></figure></div><div style="min-width:0"><h3 style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">Deformation on rear quarter panel</h3><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">A shallow deformation is visible on the rear quarter panel above the wheel arch. No paint fracture is visible at this resolution.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)"><strong style="font-weight:600">Why this confidence:</strong> The shading pattern is consistent with a dent, but a reflection or a shadow can produce a similar pattern. Confidence held low.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-2);font-size:var(--t-sm)">Deformation above the rear wheel arch <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">photo_03 [0.55, 0.40, 0.20, 0.18]</span></p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule);display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask the seller</span> Do you know how the dent on the rear quarter happened?</div></div></div></div></article><article id="vf_bay_01" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-sev-minor)"><header style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--s-3)"><span class="chip chip-solid" style="background:var(--tk-sev-minor)">minor</span><span class="label">Fluid Leak Indicator · vision</span></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="CONF 0.61"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">CONF</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-minor)">0.61</span></span></header><div class="split split-figure" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)"><div style="display:grid;gap:var(--s-3)"><figure style="margin:0"><a href="#asset-photo_08" style="display:block;text-decoration:none"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;background:#000;border:1px solid var(--tk-rule);aspect-ratio:1.5"><img src="/f/demo-01/photo_08.jpg" alt="Cropped region of photo_08: Residue on engine bay surface" style="position:absolute;width:250.0000%;height:281.2500%;left:-17.5000%;top:-51.2500%;max-width:none"/><span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:22.5000%;top:27.5000%;width:55.0000%;height:45.0000%;border:2px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.55)"><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;top:-2px;left:-2px;border-top:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-left:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;top:-2px;right:-2px;border-top:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-right:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;bottom:-2px;left:-2px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-left:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;bottom:-2px;right:-2px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-right:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span></span><span class="label" style="position:absolute;top:8px;left:8px;background:var(--tk-locked);color:var(--tk-void);font-size:9px;padding:2px 6px">Synthetic</span><span class="data" style="position:absolute;bottom:8px;right:8px;background:rgba(11,10,9,0.82);color:var(--tk-graphite);font-size:10px;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid var(--tk-rule)">2.5×</span></div></a><figcaption style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-3);margin-top:var(--s-2);font-size:var(--t-xs)"><span class="data dim">photo_08</span><span class="dim" style="text-align:right">22×16% of frame</span></figcaption></figure></div><div style="min-width:0"><h3 style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">Residue visible on engine bay surface</h3><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">A dark residue is visible on a surface in the engine bay. Whether this is an active leak, a past leak that was cleaned, or spilled fluid from a top-up cannot be determined from a photograph.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)"><strong style="font-weight:600">Why this confidence:</strong> The residue is visible but its source is not traceable in a single still image.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-2);font-size:var(--t-sm)">Residue on engine bay surface <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">photo_08 [0.16, 0.28, 0.22, 0.16]</span></p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule);display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask the seller</span> Is the engine losing any fluid? When were the fluids last topped up or changed?</div><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask a mechanic</span> Ask a mechanic to identify the fluid and find its source.</div></div></div></div></article><article id="vf_tire_01" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-sev-minor)"><header style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--s-3)"><span class="chip chip-solid" style="background:var(--tk-sev-minor)">minor</span><span class="label">Tire Tread Estimate · vision</span></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="CONF 0.58"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">CONF</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-minor)">0.58</span></span></header><div class="split split-figure" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)"><div style="display:grid;gap:var(--s-3)"><figure style="margin:0"><a href="#asset-photo_07" style="display:block;text-decoration:none"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;background:#000;border:1px solid var(--tk-rule);aspect-ratio:1.5"><img src="/f/demo-01/photo_07.jpg" alt="Cropped region of photo_07: Tread block area on the front left tire" style="position:absolute;width:135.8025%;height:152.7778%;left:-15.1852%;top:-23.3333%;max-width:none"/><span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:25.5556%;top:22.5000%;width:48.8889%;height:55.0000%;border:2px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.55)"><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;top:-2px;left:-2px;border-top:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-left:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;top:-2px;right:-2px;border-top:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-right:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;bottom:-2px;left:-2px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-left:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;bottom:-2px;right:-2px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor);border-right:3px solid var(--tk-sev-minor)"></span></span><span class="label" style="position:absolute;top:8px;left:8px;background:var(--tk-locked);color:var(--tk-void);font-size:9px;padding:2px 6px">Synthetic</span><span class="data" style="position:absolute;bottom:8px;right:8px;background:rgba(11,10,9,0.82);color:var(--tk-graphite);font-size:10px;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid var(--tk-rule)">1.4×</span></div></a><figcaption style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-3);margin-top:var(--s-2);font-size:var(--t-xs)"><span class="data dim">photo_07</span><span class="dim" style="text-align:right">36×36% of frame</span></figcaption></figure></div><div style="min-width:0"><h3 style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">Front left tread appears low</h3><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">Tread depth on the front left tire appears low relative to the tread block spacing visible in this image. Tread depth from a photograph is an estimate; a tread gauge costs a few dollars and settles it in seconds.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)"><strong style="font-weight:600">Why this confidence:</strong> Tread depth from a single photograph at this angle is unreliable. Confidence is low on purpose and this finding should be treated as a prompt to measure, not a measurement.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-2);font-size:var(--t-sm)">Tread block area on the front left tire <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">photo_07 [0.30, 0.30, 0.36, 0.36]</span></p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule);display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Est. repair</span> <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-sev-minor)">$380–$620</span></div><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask the seller</span> How old are the tires, and were they all replaced at the same time?</div><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask a mechanic</span> Measure tread depth on all four tires with a gauge and check for uneven wear that would suggest an alignment problem.</div></div></div></div></article><article id="vf_odo_01" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-sev-info)"><header style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--s-3)"><span class="chip chip-solid" style="background:var(--tk-sev-info)">info</span><span class="label">Odometer Reading · vision</span></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="CONF 0.91"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">CONF</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-line)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-info)">0.91</span></span></header><div class="split split-figure" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)"><div style="display:grid;gap:var(--s-3)"><figure style="margin:0"><a href="#asset-photo_06" style="display:block;text-decoration:none"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;background:#000;border:1px solid var(--tk-rule);aspect-ratio:1.5"><img src="/f/demo-01/photo_06.jpg" alt="Cropped region of photo_06: Odometer display reading 128,540" style="position:absolute;width:183.3333%;height:206.2500%;left:-39.8333%;top:-53.1250%;max-width:none"/><span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:22.5000%;top:37.6250%;width:55.0000%;height:24.7500%;border:2px solid var(--tk-sev-info);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.55)"><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;top:-2px;left:-2px;border-top:3px solid var(--tk-sev-info);border-left:3px solid var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;top:-2px;right:-2px;border-top:3px solid var(--tk-sev-info);border-right:3px solid var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;bottom:-2px;left:-2px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--tk-sev-info);border-left:3px solid var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;bottom:-2px;right:-2px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--tk-sev-info);border-right:3px solid var(--tk-sev-info)"></span></span><span class="label" style="position:absolute;top:8px;left:8px;background:var(--tk-locked);color:var(--tk-void);font-size:9px;padding:2px 6px">Synthetic</span><span class="data" style="position:absolute;bottom:8px;right:8px;background:rgba(11,10,9,0.82);color:var(--tk-graphite);font-size:10px;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid var(--tk-rule)">1.8×</span></div></a><figcaption style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-3);margin-top:var(--s-2);font-size:var(--t-xs)"><span class="data dim">photo_06</span><span class="dim" style="text-align:right">30×12% of frame</span></figcaption></figure></div><div style="min-width:0"><h3 style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">Odometer reads 128,540 miles</h3><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">The odometer display reads 128,540 miles in this photograph. This matches the mileage stated by the seller. A photograph of an odometer is evidence of what the display showed when the photo was taken, and nothing more.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)"><strong style="font-weight:600">Why this confidence:</strong> All digits are legible and unobstructed. Confidence reflects the legibility of the display, not the truthfulness of the reading.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-2);font-size:var(--t-sm)">Odometer display reading 128,540 <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">photo_06 [0.34, 0.44, 0.30, 0.12]</span></p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule);display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask the seller</span> Can you show me the title and any service records so I can check the mileage history?</div></div></div></div></article></div></section><section class="section" id="recalls"><div class="section-label"><span>On record for this model (6)</span><span class="dim" style="letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:none">not about this specific car</span></div><div class="panel panel-edge prose-sm" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-locked);margin-bottom:var(--s-4)">These describe the model and year, not the car you are looking at. They are not counted in the red-flag score. Recall work is free at a dealer, and a dealer will tell you by VIN whether it was done on this specific vehicle — which is something no public database publishes and this report cannot know.</div><div style="display:grid;gap:var(--s-4)"><article id="recall_25V422000" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-sev-major)"><header style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--s-3)"><span class="chip chip-solid" style="background:var(--tk-sev-major)">major</span><span class="label">Open Recall · data</span></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="CONF 1.00"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">CONF</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-major)">1.00</span></span></header><div class="split" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)"><div style="min-width:0"><h3 style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">Recall 25V422000: POWER TRAIN:DRIVELINE:DRIVESHAFT</h3><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2013 Honda Accord vehicles equipped with a 4-cylinder engine and a continuously-variable transmission. The affected vehicles were originally sold, or ever registered, in Connecticut, Delaware, District of Columbia, Illinois, Indiana, Iowa, Kentucky, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Minnesota, Missouri, New Hampshire, New Jersey, New York, Ohio, Pennsylvania, Rhode Island, Vermont, Virginia, West Virginia, and Wisconsin. The driveshaft may corrode and break, due to damage from road salt or other contaminants. NHTSA states the consequence: A broken driveshaft can result in a loss of drive power, or a vehicle rollaway when the vehicle is in park without the parking brake applied. Both scenarios can increase the risk of a crash or injury. This campaign is on record for this model year. TIREKICK cannot tell whether it was ever carried out on this particular vehicle - NHTSA does not publish per-VIN repair status - so treat it as a question to settle, not as a defect found. Any dealer will check by VIN and perform outstanding recall work free.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)"><strong style="font-weight:600">Why this confidence:</strong> Transcribed from the NHTSA recall record, not judged by a model. The certainty is that this campaign exists and covers this model year. Whether it is outstanding on this car is not something we know.</p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule)"><div class="label">Evidence</div><ul class="prose-sm" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 0;padding-left:var(--s-5)"><li class="dim" style="margin-bottom:var(--s-1)"><span style="color:var(--tk-paper)">NHTSA Safety Recalls</span> / <span class="data">25V422000</span> — NHTSA campaign 25V422000 - POWER TRAIN:DRIVELINE:DRIVESHAFT <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">(2026-07-26T23:31:29Z)</span></li></ul></div><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule);display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask the seller</span> Recall 25V422000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</div></div></div></div></article><article id="recall_23V858000" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-sev-major)"><header style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--s-3)"><span class="chip chip-solid" style="background:var(--tk-sev-major)">major</span><span class="label">Open Recall · data</span></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="CONF 1.00"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">CONF</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-major)">1.00</span></span></header><div class="split" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)"><div style="min-width:0"><h3 style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">Recall 23V858000: FUEL SYSTEM, GASOLINE:DELIVERY:FUEL PUMP</h3><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2013-2023 Honda Accord, Civic Coupe, Civic Sedan, Civic Hatchback, Civic Type R, CR-V, HR-V, Ridgeline, Odyssey, Acura ILX, MDX, MDX Hybrid, RDX, RLX, TLX, 2019-2022 Honda Insight, Passport, 2020 Honda CR-V Hybrid, 2018-2019 Honda Clarity PHEV, Fit, and 2015-2020 Honda Accord Hybrid, Pilot, Acura NSX vehicles.  The fuel pump inside the fuel tank may fail. NHTSA states the consequence: Fuel pump failure can cause an engine stall while driving, increasing the risk of a crash. This campaign is on record for this model year. TIREKICK cannot tell whether it was ever carried out on this particular vehicle - NHTSA does not publish per-VIN repair status - so treat it as a question to settle, not as a defect found. Any dealer will check by VIN and perform outstanding recall work free.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)"><strong style="font-weight:600">Why this confidence:</strong> Transcribed from the NHTSA recall record, not judged by a model. The certainty is that this campaign exists and covers this model year. Whether it is outstanding on this car is not something we know.</p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule)"><div class="label">Evidence</div><ul class="prose-sm" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 0;padding-left:var(--s-5)"><li class="dim" style="margin-bottom:var(--s-1)"><span style="color:var(--tk-paper)">NHTSA Safety Recalls</span> / <span class="data">23V858000</span> — NHTSA campaign 23V858000 - FUEL SYSTEM, GASOLINE:DELIVERY:FUEL PUMP <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">(2026-07-26T23:31:29Z)</span></li></ul></div><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule);display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask the seller</span> Recall 23V858000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</div></div></div></div></article><article id="recall_20V769000" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-sev-major)"><header style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--s-3)"><span class="chip chip-solid" style="background:var(--tk-sev-major)">major</span><span class="label">Open Recall · data</span></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="CONF 1.00"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">CONF</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-major)">1.00</span></span></header><div class="split" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)"><div style="min-width:0"><h3 style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">Recall 20V769000: POWER TRAIN:DRIVELINE:DRIVESHAFT</h3><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2013-2015 Accord vehicles equipped with a 4-cylinder engine and a continuously-variable transmission that were originally sold, or ever registered, in Connecticut, Delaware, District of Columbia, Illinois, Indiana, Iowa, Kentucky, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Minnesota, Missouri, New Hampshire, New Jersey, New York, Ohio, Pennsylvania, Rhode Island, Vermont, Virginia, West Virginia, and Wisconsin.  The drive shafts were assembled with a lubricant that may have degraded the drive shafts&#x27; protective coating, making it more susceptible to damage from road salt or other contaminants, and potentially cause it to break. NHTSA states the consequence: A broken drive shaft may cause a sudden loss of drive power.  The vehicle could also roll away if the parking brake has not been applied before the vehicle has been exited.  Either condition can increase the risk of a crash or injury. This campaign is on record for this model year. TIREKICK cannot tell whether it was ever carried out on this particular vehicle - NHTSA does not publish per-VIN repair status - so treat it as a question to settle, not as a defect found. Any dealer will check by VIN and perform outstanding recall work free.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)"><strong style="font-weight:600">Why this confidence:</strong> Transcribed from the NHTSA recall record, not judged by a model. The certainty is that this campaign exists and covers this model year. Whether it is outstanding on this car is not something we know.</p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule)"><div class="label">Evidence</div><ul class="prose-sm" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 0;padding-left:var(--s-5)"><li class="dim" style="margin-bottom:var(--s-1)"><span style="color:var(--tk-paper)">NHTSA Safety Recalls</span> / <span class="data">20V769000</span> — NHTSA campaign 20V769000 - POWER TRAIN:DRIVELINE:DRIVESHAFT <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">(2026-07-26T23:31:29Z)</span></li></ul></div><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule);display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask the seller</span> Recall 20V769000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</div></div></div></div></article><article id="recall_17V418000" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-sev-major)"><header style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--s-3)"><span class="chip chip-solid" style="background:var(--tk-sev-major)">major</span><span class="label">Open Recall · data</span></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="CONF 1.00"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">CONF</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-major)">1.00</span></span></header><div class="split" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)"><div style="min-width:0"><h3 style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">Recall 17V418000: ELECTRICAL SYSTEM:12V/24V/48V BATTERY</h3><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2013-2016 Honda Accord vehicles.  The case for the battery sensor, part of the battery management system, may allow water to get in, potentially causing an electrical short. NHTSA states the consequence: An electrical short increases the risk of a fire. This campaign is on record for this model year. TIREKICK cannot tell whether it was ever carried out on this particular vehicle - NHTSA does not publish per-VIN repair status - so treat it as a question to settle, not as a defect found. Any dealer will check by VIN and perform outstanding recall work free.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)"><strong style="font-weight:600">Why this confidence:</strong> Transcribed from the NHTSA recall record, not judged by a model. The certainty is that this campaign exists and covers this model year. Whether it is outstanding on this car is not something we know.</p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule)"><div class="label">Evidence</div><ul class="prose-sm" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 0;padding-left:var(--s-5)"><li class="dim" style="margin-bottom:var(--s-1)"><span style="color:var(--tk-paper)">NHTSA Safety Recalls</span> / <span class="data">17V418000</span> — NHTSA campaign 17V418000 - ELECTRICAL SYSTEM:12V/24V/48V BATTERY <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">(2026-07-26T23:31:29Z)</span></li></ul></div><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule);display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask the seller</span> Recall 17V418000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</div></div></div></div></article><article id="recall_13V297000" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-sev-major)"><header style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--s-3)"><span class="chip chip-solid" style="background:var(--tk-sev-major)">major</span><span class="label">Open Recall · data</span></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="CONF 1.00"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">CONF</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-major)">1.00</span></span></header><div class="split" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)"><div style="min-width:0"><h3 style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">Recall 13V297000: FUEL SYSTEM, GASOLINE</h3><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">American Honda Motor Co., Inc. (Honda) is recalling certain model year 2013 Accord vehicles that are Low-Emission Vehicle (LEV) II rated that were manufactured January 15, 2013, through April 5, 2013.  The fuel tank neck may be out of specification causing the fuel pump to not properly seal to the fuel tank. NHTSA states the consequence: An insufficent seal may led to a fuel leak which increases the risk of a fire. This campaign is on record for this model year. TIREKICK cannot tell whether it was ever carried out on this particular vehicle - NHTSA does not publish per-VIN repair status - so treat it as a question to settle, not as a defect found. Any dealer will check by VIN and perform outstanding recall work free.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)"><strong style="font-weight:600">Why this confidence:</strong> Transcribed from the NHTSA recall record, not judged by a model. The certainty is that this campaign exists and covers this model year. Whether it is outstanding on this car is not something we know.</p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule)"><div class="label">Evidence</div><ul class="prose-sm" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 0;padding-left:var(--s-5)"><li class="dim" style="margin-bottom:var(--s-1)"><span style="color:var(--tk-paper)">NHTSA Safety Recalls</span> / <span class="data">13V297000</span> — NHTSA campaign 13V297000 - FUEL SYSTEM, GASOLINE <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">(2026-07-26T23:31:29Z)</span></li></ul></div><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule);display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask the seller</span> Recall 13V297000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</div></div></div></div></article><article id="complaint_pattern_summary" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-sev-info)"><header style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--s-3)"><span class="chip chip-solid" style="background:var(--tk-sev-info)">info</span><span class="label">Complaint Pattern · data</span></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="CONF 1.00"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">CONF</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-info)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-info)">1.00</span></span></header><div class="split" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)"><div style="min-width:0"><h3 style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">What owners of the 2013 HONDA Accord complain about</h3><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">1,418 owners filed complaints with NHTSA about the 2013 HONDA Accord. The most reported areas were steering (497), electrical system (413), engine (179), unknown or other (118). This is a pattern across the model, not an observation about this car - a popular car accumulates complaints simply by being everywhere. Use it as a list of things to look at closely and ask about.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)"><strong style="font-weight:600">Why this confidence:</strong> A count of public records, not a judgment. What is certain is the number of complaints filed about this model year. Nothing here is evidence about the vehicle you are looking at.</p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule)"><div class="label">Evidence</div><ul class="prose-sm" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 0;padding-left:var(--s-5)"><li class="dim" style="margin-bottom:var(--s-1)"><span style="color:var(--tk-paper)">NHTSA Owner Complaints</span> / <span class="data">complaints/2013-HONDA-Accord</span> — 1,418 owner complaints on file for the 2013 HONDA Accord <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">(2026-07-26T23:31:36Z)</span></li></ul></div><div style="margin-top:var(--s-4);padding-top:var(--s-3);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule);display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask the seller</span> Owners of this model most often report problems with steering. Has this car had any work done there?</div><div class="prose-sm"><span class="label">Ask a mechanic</span> Ask a mechanic to pay particular attention to steering on this model.</div></div></div></div></article></div></section><section class="section" id="mechanic"><div class="section-label"><span>For your mechanic (2)</span><span class="dim" style="letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:none">locked systems - observation only, no severity, no confidence</span></div><div style="display:grid;gap:var(--s-3)"><div id="ref_vf_bay_02" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-locked)"><div class="label" style="color:var(--tk-locked)">brakes</div><p class="prose" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 var(--s-3)">A wet area is visible on and around the front hub assembly.</p><p class="prose-sm muted" style="margin:0">Ask an independent mechanic to inspect this on a lift before you buy. TIREKICK cannot assess it from photos, video, or audio.</p></div><div id="ref_title_structural_history_01" class="panel panel-edge" style="border-left-color:var(--tk-locked)"><div class="label" style="color:var(--tk-locked)">structure</div><p class="prose" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 var(--s-3)">A document you uploaded reports frame or structural damage. The line is quoted below exactly as it appears. Structural repair quality cannot be assessed from paperwork or from photographs. TIREKICK did not query any title registry - this is a reading of your own paperwork, and paperwork can be incomplete or forged. Confirm the brand with your state&#x27;s motor vehicle agency before you buy, and price the car as branded until you have.</p><p class="prose-sm muted" style="margin:0">Ask an independent mechanic to inspect this on a lift before you buy. TIREKICK cannot assess it from photos, video, or audio.</p></div></div></section><section class="section" id="walkaround"><div class="section-label"><span>Walkaround video</span><span class="dim" style="letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:none">what was kept, and what was thrown away</span></div><div class="panel"><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(130px, 100%), 1fr));gap:var(--s-4)"><div><div class="label">Video length</div><div class="data" style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">14.0s</div></div><div><div class="label">Frames sampled</div><div class="data" style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">28</div></div><div><div class="label">Frames analysed</div><div class="data" style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">5</div></div><div><div class="label">Dropped - too blurred</div><div class="data" style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">4</div></div><div><div class="label">Dropped - duplicate view</div><div class="data" style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">4</div></div><div><div class="label">Dropped - over the cap</div><div class="data" style="font-size:var(--t-lg)">0</div></div></div><p class="prose-sm muted" style="margin-top:var(--s-5)">5 frame(s) were taken from 14 seconds of video and analysed as photographs. 4 were too blurred to read - a blurred frame is worse than no frame, because it is the input most likely to turn a shadow into a dent. 4 showed the same view as a frame already chosen.</p><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-3)">Frames kept from <span class="data">0.0s, 2.0s, 3.5s, 8.5s, 13.5s</span>. Each was then classified and analysed exactly as an uploaded photograph would have been.</p></div></section><section class="section" id="gallery"><div class="section-label"><span>All media (13)</span><span class="dim" style="letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:none">every image, whether anything was found on it or not</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(300px, 100%), 1fr));gap:var(--s-5)"><div id="asset-photo_01" class="section"><figure style="margin:0"><div style="position:relative;background:#000;border:1px solid var(--tk-line);line-height:0"><img src="/f/demo-01/photo_01.jpg" alt="exterior_side_left - photo_01" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;filter:saturate(0.85) brightness(0.92)"/><span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;inset:0;pointer-events:none;background-image:repeating-linear-gradient(to right, rgba(230,237,243,0.04) 0 1px, transparent 1px 40px),repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(230,237,243,0.04) 0 1px, transparent 1px 40px)"></span><a href="#vf_rust_01" title="Corrosion band along the lower rocker panel" style="position:absolute;left:8.000%;top:62.000%;width:34.000%;height:14.000%;border:2px solid var(--tk-sev-major);background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--tk-sev-major) 8%, transparent);border-radius:0;display:block"><span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;width:9px;height:9px;top:-2px;left:-2px;border-top:2px solid var(--tk-sev-major);border-left:2px solid var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;width:9px;height:9px;top:-2px;right:-2px;border-top:2px solid var(--tk-sev-major);border-right:2px solid var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;width:9px;height:9px;bottom:-2px;left:-2px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--tk-sev-major);border-left:2px solid var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;width:9px;height:9px;bottom:-2px;right:-2px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--tk-sev-major);border-right:2px solid var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="position:absolute;top:100%;margin-top:4px;left:-2px;background:var(--tk-sev-major);color:#0a0c0e;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.12em;padding:2px 6px;white-space:nowrap;line-height:1.6">RUST CORROSION / MAJOR / 0.72<