ose-sm">Not remotely verifiable - independent mechanic required.</div></td></tr><tr><td class="label" style="color:var(--tk-paper)">structure</td><td><span class="chip" style="color:var(--tk-locked)">MECHANIC REQUIRED</span></td><td style="color:var(--tk-locked)"><div class="prose-sm">Not remotely verifiable - independent mechanic required.</div></td></tr><tr><td class="label" style="color:var(--tk-paper)">fluids</td><td><span class="chip" style="color:var(--tk-unknown)">CANNOT DETERMINE</span></td><td><div class="prose-sm">Cannot be determined from photographs, video, or audio. Assessing fluids requires a test drive or a lift.</div></td></tr><tr><td class="label" style="color:var(--tk-paper)">glass</td><td><span class="chip" style="color:var(--tk-unknown)">CANNOT DETERMINE</span></td><td><div class="prose-sm">Cannot be determined - TIREKICK has no analysis pass that assesses glass from photographs. The media may show it; we did not examine it.</div></td></tr><tr><td class="label" style="color:var(--tk-paper)">documentation</td><td><span class="chip" style="color:var(--tk-sev-major)">ATTENTION</span></td><td><div class="prose-sm">Hail damage reported in your documents (and 1 more)<span style="margin-left:var(--s-3);display:inline-block"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px" title="MAX 1.00"><span class="mono-label" style="letter-spacing:0.12em">MAX</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:2px" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span><span style="width:7px;height:12px;background:var(--tk-sev-major)"></span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--tk-sev-major)">1.00</span></span></span></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)">The four rows marked not remotely verifiable - independent mechanic required are locked in software. TIREKICK will not report on them at any confidence, on any vehicle, ever.</p></section><section class="section" id="audio"><div class="section-label"><span>Engine audio</span></div><div class="panel"><div class="prose" style="border:1px solid var(--tk-locked);border-left-width:4px;background:rgba(163,113,247,0.07);padding:14px 16px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:20px">TIREKICK does not make claims about engine condition from audio. The anomaly detector has not been measured against a labelled set, so under our own accuracy rules it cannot appear in a report. What is below is the recording itself, drawn as a spectrogram, and the measurements taken from it. Listen to the clip yourself, and play it to a mechanic at a cold start.</div><figure style="margin:0"><div style="position:relative;border:1px solid var(--tk-line);line-height:0"><img src="/f/demo-01/audio_01.spectrogram.png" alt="Spectrogram of audio_01" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block"/><div><div style="position:absolute;left:22.64090909090909%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:var(--tk-sev-major);opacity:0.85"></div><div style="position:absolute;left:22.64090909090909%;top:4px;transform:translateX(-50%);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:var(--tk-sev-major);background:rgba(10,12,14,0.75);padding:1px 4px;white-space:nowrap">5.0s</div></div><div><div style="position:absolute;left:52.19090909090909%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:var(--tk-sev-major);opacity:0.85"></div><div style="position:absolute;left:52.19090909090909%;top:4px;transform:translateX(-50%);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:var(--tk-sev-major);background:rgba(10,12,14,0.75);padding:1px 4px;white-space:nowrap">11.5s</div></div><div><div style="position:absolute;left:78.31363636363636%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:var(--tk-sev-major);opacity:0.85"></div><div style="position:absolute;left:78.31363636363636%;top:4px;transform:translateX(-50%);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:var(--tk-sev-major);background:rgba(10,12,14,0.75);padding:1px 4px;white-space:nowrap">17.2s</div></div></div><figcaption style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-top:6px;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--tk-unknown)"><span>0s</span><span>frequency, low at bottom / log scale</span><span>22s</span></figcaption></figure><audio controls="" preload="none" src="/f/demo-01/audio_01.wav" style="width:100%;margin-top:16px;color-scheme:dark">Your browser cannot play this audio clip.</audio><div class="prose" style="font-size:13px;margin-top:18px">3 sharp transient(s) stand out from the rest of the recording, at 5.0s, 11.5s, 17.2s of 22s. A transient is a sudden broadband sound. It could be a mechanical tick. It could equally be a door, a footstep, or the phone brushing a sleeve. TIREKICK is showing you where to listen, not telling you what it heard.</div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(140px, 100%), 1fr));gap:16px;margin-top:20px;padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid var(--tk-line)"><div><div class="mono-label">Length</div><div style="font-size:18px">22.0s</div></div><div><div class="mono-label">Dominant tone</div><div style="font-size:18px">32.3 Hz</div></div><div><div class="mono-label">Implied idle</div><div style="font-size:18px">969 rpm</div></div><div><div class="mono-label">Level</div><div style="font-size:18px">-25 dBFS</div></div><div><div class="mono-label">Clipped</div><div style="font-size:18px">0.0%</div></div></div><div class="prose muted" style="font-size:12px;margin-top:14px">The loudest steady tone is 32.3Hz. A four-stroke 4-cylinder engine fires 2 times per revolution, which puts this at about 969 rpm. That is arithmetic on the recording, not a reading from the vehicle.</div></div></section><section class="section" id="record"><div class="section-label"><span>Vehicle record</span></div><div class="panel"><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(140px, 100%), 1fr));gap:var(--s-4)"><div><div class="label">VIN</div><div class="data">1HGCR2F37DA******</div></div><div><div class="label">Year</div><div class="data">2013</div></div><div><div class="label">Make</div><div class="data">HONDA</div></div><div><div class="label">Model</div><div class="data">Accord</div></div><div><div class="label">Trim</div><div class="data">LX</div></div><div><div class="label">Engine</div><div class="data">2.4L 4-cyl K24W1</div></div><div><div class="label">Drive</div><div class="data">—</div></div><div><div class="label">Body</div><div class="data">Sedan/Saloon</div></div></div><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-5)">VIN is 17 characters and passes its position-9 check digit, so it is internally consistent. That confirms the number was transcribed correctly. It does not confirm the number belongs to the car in the photographs.</p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-5);padding-top:var(--s-4);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule)"><div class="label" style="color:var(--tk-locked)">Recalls — what this list is</div><p class="prose-sm" style="margin-top:var(--s-2);color:var(--tk-locked)">5 recall campaign(s) on record for the 2013 HONDA Accord. NHTSA publishes recalls by model, not by VIN, and does not publish whether a campaign was carried out on any individual vehicle. So this is a list of what could apply to this car - not a list of what is outstanding on it. A dealer can tell you, by VIN, in a phone call, and the work is free.</p></div><div style="margin-top:var(--s-5)"><div class="label">Owner complaints for this model</div><div style="display:flex;gap:var(--s-6);flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:var(--s-3)"><div><div class="data" style="font-size:var(--t-xl)">1,418</div><div class="label">complaints filed</div></div><div style="flex:1 1 320px;min-width:0"><div style="display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><div style="display:grid;gap:3px"><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-3);font-size:var(--t-sm)"><span>STEERING</span><span class="data dim">497</span></div><div style="height:4px;background:var(--tk-rule)"><div style="width:100%;height:100%;background:var(--tk-graphite)"></div></div></div><div style="display:grid;gap:3px"><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-3);font-size:var(--t-sm)"><span>ELECTRICAL SYSTEM</span><span class="data dim">413</span></div><div style="height:4px;background:var(--tk-rule)"><div style="width:83.09859154929578%;height:100%;background:var(--tk-graphite)"></div></div></div><div style="display:grid;gap:3px"><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-3);font-size:var(--t-sm)"><span>ENGINE</span><span class="data dim">179</span></div><div style="height:4px;background:var(--tk-rule)"><div style="width:36.016096579476866%;height:100%;background:var(--tk-graphite)"></div></div></div><div style="display:grid;gap:3px"><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-3);font-size:var(--t-sm)"><span>UNKNOWN OR OTHER</span><span class="data dim">118</span></div><div style="height:4px;background:var(--tk-rule)"><div style="width:23.74245472837022%;height:100%;background:var(--tk-graphite)"></div></div></div><div style="display:grid;gap:3px"><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-3);font-size:var(--t-sm)"><span>SERVICE BRAKES</span><span class="data dim">115</span></div><div style="height:4px;background:var(--tk-rule)"><div style="width:23.138832997987926%;height:100%;background:var(--tk-graphite)"></div></div></div><div style="display:grid;gap:3px"><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-3);font-size:var(--t-sm)"><span>POWER TRAIN</span><span class="data dim">109</span></div><div style="height:4px;background:var(--tk-rule)"><div style="width:21.93158953722334%;height:100%;background:var(--tk-graphite)"></div></div></div></div></div></div><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-4)">Complaints filed with NHTSA by owners of the 2013 HONDA Accord, across the whole model year. They describe the model. None of them describes this car, and a high count on a common vehicle is partly just a high count of vehicles.</p></div><div style="margin-top:var(--s-5);padding-top:var(--s-4);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule)"><div class="label">Sources</div><ul style="margin:var(--s-3) 0 0;padding-left:var(--s-5)"><li class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-bottom:var(--s-2)"><span style="color:var(--tk-paper)">NHTSA vPIC</span> <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">(retrieved 2026-07-26T23:31:29Z)</span><div>What the manufacturer encoded into this VIN. It describes how the vehicle left the factory, not its condition today.</div></li><li class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-bottom:var(--s-2)"><span style="color:var(--tk-paper)">NHTSA Safety Recalls</span> <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">(retrieved 2026-07-26T23:31:29Z)</span><div>Every safety recall campaign NHTSA has filed against the 2013 HONDA Accord. Keyed to the model, not to this VIN.</div></li><li class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-bottom:var(--s-2)"><span style="color:var(--tk-paper)">NHTSA Owner Complaints</span> <span class="data" style="color:var(--tk-pencil)">(retrieved 2026-07-26T23:31:36Z)</span><div>Owner-filed complaint counts for the 2013 HONDA ACCORD. Counts only - the narratives belong to the people who wrote them and are not retained.</div></li></ul></div></div></section><section class="section" id="price"><div class="section-label"><span>Price check</span></div><div class="panel"><div style="display:flex;gap:var(--s-7);flex-wrap:wrap"><div><div class="label">Asking</div><div class="data" style="font-size:var(--t-xl)">$8,900</div></div><div><div class="label">Supported by these comps</div><div class="data" style="font-size:var(--t-xl)">$6,928–$7,568</div></div><div><div class="label">Verdict</div><span class="chip" style="color:var(--tk-sev-major);font-size:var(--t-xs)">above range</span></div></div><p class="prose" style="margin-top:var(--s-5)">The asking price of $8,900 is above the $6,928-$7,568 range these comparable listings support after the deductions above. The gap is $1,332.</p><div style="margin-top:var(--s-6)"><div class="label">The comps behind this range</div><div class="table-scroll"><table style="margin-top:var(--s-2)"><thead><tr><th>Listing</th><th>Year / trim</th><th>Mileage</th><th>Asking</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div class="prose-sm dim">Pasted by the buyer - local listing, same model year, LX trim</div></td><td>2013 LX</td><td class="data">112,300</td><td class="data">$9,400</td></tr><tr><td><div class="prose-sm dim">Pasted by the buyer - local listing, same model year</div></td><td>2013 LX</td><td class="data">134,800</td><td class="data">$8,100</td></tr><tr><td><div class="prose-sm dim">Pasted by the buyer - listing 40 miles away, lower mileage</div></td><td>2013 EX</td><td class="data">98,500</td><td class="data">$10,200</td></tr><tr><td><div class="prose-sm dim">Pasted by the buyer - high-mileage example, same trim</div></td><td>2013 LX</td><td class="data">151,000</td><td class="data">$7,300</td></tr><tr><td><div class="prose-sm dim">Pasted by the buyer - similar price, different car</div></td><td>2013 EX</td><td class="data">121,000</td><td class="data">$8,750</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div style="margin-top:var(--s-6)"><div class="label" style="color:var(--tk-unknown)">Listings you gave us that were left out, and why</div><div class="table-scroll"><table style="margin-top:var(--s-2)"><tbody><tr><td class="data" style="white-space:nowrap">comp_5</td><td><div class="prose-sm dim">listed as a Civic; this vehicle is a Accord</div></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div style="margin-top:var(--s-6)"><div class="label">Deductions, each linked to a finding</div><div class="table-scroll"><table style="margin-top:var(--s-2)"><tbody><tr><td><a href="#vf_rust_01">Corrosion visible along driver-side rocker panel</a></td><td class="data" style="color:var(--tk-sev-major);white-space:nowrap">−$600 to −$900</td><td><div class="prose-sm dim">Repair cost band attached to this finding. Confidence in the finding itself is 0.72.</div></td></tr><tr><td><a href="#vf_tire_01">Front left tread appears low</a></td><td class="data" style="color:var(--tk-sev-major);white-space:nowrap">−$380 to −$620</td><td><div class="prose-sm dim">Repair cost band attached to this finding. Confidence in the finding itself is 0.58.</div></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p class="prose-sm dim" style="margin-top:var(--s-5)">Mileage adjustment of $-0.056 per mile, fitted from the 4 comparable listings provided rather than from any assumed depreciation rate. Range built from 4 listing(s) you provided. It reflects those listings and nothing else - not a market index, not an appraisal. Asking prices, not sale prices. What a car is listed at and what it sells for are different numbers, and the second one is not public. 1 listing(s) you provided were left out of the range as comparisons for a different vehicle. They are listed above with the reason. 1 of 4 dated listing(s) are more than 90 days old. They are still counted - they are your research - but they describe an older market than the one you are buying in. Subject mileage of 128,540 is as stated by the seller and has not been verified.</p></div></section><section class="section" id="questions"><div class="section-label"><span>Questions for the seller (18)</span></div><ol class="prose-sm" style="padding-left:var(--s-5);display:grid;gap:var(--s-2)"><li>How long has the rust on the rocker panel been there, and has any bodywork been done to it?</li><li>Do you know how the dent on the rear quarter happened?</li><li>The check-engine light is on in your photo. What code is it throwing, and how long has it been on?</li><li>Can you show me the title and any service records so I can check the mileage history?</li><li>How old are the tires, and were they all replaced at the same time?</li><li>Is the engine losing any fluid? When were the fluids last topped up or changed?</li><li>Recall 25V422000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</li><li>Recall 23V858000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</li><li>Recall 20V769000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</li><li>Recall 17V418000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</li><li>Recall 13V297000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</li><li>Owners of this model most often report problems with steering. Has this car had any work done there?</li><li>My paperwork mentions hail damage. Can you walk me through what happened, and show me the title itself?</li><li>Do you have service records? Can I see them before I come out?</li><li>Has this car been in any accident, reported or not?</li><li>Are you the titleholder, and is the title in hand and clear?</li><li>Can I take it to my mechanic for a pre-purchase inspection?</li><li>Has any recall work been done on this car? A dealer will check by VIN and do outstanding recall work free - can you show me the paperwork?</li></ol></section><section class="section" id="script"><div class="section-label"><span>Negotiation script</span></div><div style="display:grid;gap:var(--s-3)"><div class="panel"><div class="label">Open by naming what you did</div><p class="prose" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 0">“I ran the photos and the VIN through an AI analysis before coming out. It flagged a few things I want to look at with you.”</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="label">Raise: Corrosion visible along driver-side rocker panel</div><p class="prose" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 0">“The analysis flagged corrosion visible along driver-side rocker panel, and put a rough band of $600 to $900 on that kind of work - its own estimate, not a quote. I&#x27;d want a shop to price it properly. Can we talk about the price with that in mind?”</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="label">Raise: Front left tread appears low</div><p class="prose" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 0">“The analysis flagged front left tread appears low, and put a rough band of $380 to $620 on that kind of work - its own estimate, not a quote. I&#x27;d want a shop to price it properly. Can we talk about the price with that in mind?”</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="label">Anchor on the comps</div><p class="prose" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 0">“I looked at comparable listings and they support roughly $6,928 to $7,568 for this car in this condition. Here are the listings I looked at. Can you meet me in that range?”</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="label">Protect yourself on what the analysis could not see</div><p class="prose" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 0">“The analysis was clear that it can&#x27;t assess brakes, airbags, frame, or steering from photos. I&#x27;d like to take it to my mechanic before we finalize. If that&#x27;s not possible, I understand, but then I&#x27;d need the price to reflect the risk I&#x27;m taking on.”</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="label">Be willing to leave</div><p class="prose" style="margin:var(--s-2) 0 0">“I appreciate your time. Let me think it over and I&#x27;ll call you tomorrow.”</p></div></div></section><section class="section" id="run"><div class="section-label"><span>Run metadata</span></div><div class="table-scroll"><table><tbody><tr><td class="label">Mode</td><td class="data">fixture</td></tr><tr><td class="label">Images analyzed</td><td class="data">29</td></tr><tr><td class="label">Tokens</td><td class="data">0 in / 0 out</td></tr><tr><td class="label">Audio processed</td><td class="data">22.0s</td></tr><tr><td class="label">Cost to produce</td><td class="data">$0.0000</td></tr><tr><td class="label">Note</td><td><div class="prose-sm dim">Fixture mode: responses served from cache, no API calls billed. $0.00 is the true cost of this run and not a placeholder.</div></td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><footer style="margin-top:var(--s-9);padding-top:var(--s-5);border-top:1px solid var(--tk-rule);display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--s-4);flex-wrap:wrap"><span class="label">ANALYZED BY TIREKICK AI</span><span class="prose-sm dim" style="max-width:62ch">Automated analysis of buyer-supplied media. Not an inspection. Have an independent mechanic examine any vehicle before you buy it. <a href="/accuracy">Accuracy and known limits</a>.</span></footer></div>"`;
